PROBLEM="Define a Money value type with value-based equality and a non-mutating WithAmount(amount) that returns a copy."
LEARNINGS="Use a positional 'record' for value objects: it gives VALUE equality (two records with equal fields are Equal) for free, unlike a class (reference equality). Copy-and-modify with the 'with' expression: 'this with { Amount = amount }' returns a NEW record, leaving the original unchanged (immutability)."
ERRORS="Do NOT use a class for a value object expecting ==/Equals to compare by value (class is reference equality). Do NOT mutate fields in place; records are immutable - use 'with'."
TAGS="src:context7 lang:csharp area:language"
REF_SRC="Money.cs"
